        "passages": [
          {
            "id": "p1",
            "locator": "article/heading/page",
            "text": "When you use network security groups for network access control between subnets, you can put resources that belong to the same security zone or role in their own subnets."
          }
        ],
        "quotationMatchPolicy": "unicode-typography-v1",
        "typographyNormalizedPassages": []
      },
      "5-source-2": {
        "type": "guidance",
        "title": "Zero Trust Microsegmentation Guidance",
        "publisher": "Cloud Security Alliance",
        "url": "https://cloudsecurityalliance.org/artifacts/zero-trust-microsegmentation-guidance",
        "language": "en",
        "jurisdiction": "International",
        "applicability": "General zero trust microsegmentation controls including firewalls and ACLs",
        "publicationDate": null,
        "effectiveDate": null,
        "redistribution": "metadata-and-short-passages",
        "id": "5-source-2",
        "byteDigest": "sha256:2a5c2762cb70384bf506bd1dde35e16dd0f5b44c7b0bcda400826531302f2db0",
        "textDigest": "sha256:f09ee2b2e5f37d59bee32635dd85a885204ae945d01fd6a7a240a30811e53ff9",
        "finalUrl": "https://cloudsecurityalliance.org/artifacts/zero-trust-microsegmentation-guidance",
        "retrievedAt": "2026-10-15T21:24:39Z",
        "contentType": "text/html; charset=utf-8",
        "snapshotPath": "source-2a5c2762cb70384bf506bd1dde35e16dd0f5b44c7b0bcda400826531302f2db0.bin",
        "textPath": "source-f09ee2b2e5f37d59bee32635dd85a885204ae945d01fd6a7a240a30811e53ff9.txt",
        "sourceStatus": "fetched-and-passage-checked",
        "passages": [
          {
            "id": "p1",
            "locator": "article/heading/page",
            "text": "Microsegmentation is a foundational Zero Trust strategy that enforces explicit, fine-grained communication controls between systems. By reducing unnecessary reachability, it aids with lateral movement prevention, contains threats, and minimizes blast radius."
          },
          {
            "id": "p2",
            "locator": "article/heading/page",
            "text": "Boundaries may be expressed through zones, routes, VLANs/VXLANs, security groups, labels, tags, Kubernetes network policies, host controls, hypervisor controls, firewalls, gateways, or other enforcement points. This model is often strongest for deterministic containment, local east-west control, regulatory boundaries, and OT/ICS zones and conduits."
          }
        ],
        "quotationMatchPolicy": "unicode-typography-v1",
        "typographyNormalizedPassages": []
      },
      "5-source-3": {
        "type": "technical-doc",
        "title": "Network and Environment Capabilities",
        "publisher": "National Security Agency",
        "url": "https://www.nsa.gov/Cybersecurity/ZIG/Capabilities/Network-and-Environment/",
        "language": "en",
        "jurisdiction": "US",
        "applicability": "US Department of Defense Zero Trust Framework implementation",
        "publicationDate": null,
        "effectiveDate": null,
        "redistribution": "metadata-and-short-passages",
        "id": "5-source-3",
        "byteDigest": "sha256:458c74a40d598b2fc942b6a20c277c47f698962ae67f884ae1dcd45f222f9e05",
        "textDigest": "sha256:afe10b60f1bdc96c72326874b3aae37a4653d17a9be4e917f6e6dd070c8b62bd",
        "finalUrl": "https://www.nsa.gov/Cybersecurity/ZIG/Capabilities/Network-and-Environment/",
        "retrievedAt": "2026-10-15T21:24:42Z",
        "contentType": "text/html; charset=utf-8",
        "snapshotPath": "source-458c74a40d598b2fc942b6a20c277c47f698962ae67f884ae1dcd45f222f9e05.bin",
        "textPath": "source-afe10b60f1bdc96c72326874b3aae37a4653d17a9be4e917f6e6dd070c8b62bd.txt",
        "sourceStatus": "fetched-and-passage-checked",
        "passages": [
          {
            "id": "p1",
            "locator": "article/heading/page",
            "text": "Tailor the control access policies to address each driver's specifics, whether for regulatory compliance or data security requirements."
          },
          {
            "id": "p2",
            "locator": "article/heading/page",
            "text": "Role-Based Access Control (RBAC), where permissions are assigned based on the role of the User/PE/NPE. Attribute-Based Access Control (ABAC), where a combination of several factors related to User/PE/NPE, data, and the environment are leveraged to restrict or allow network access based on a set of predefined rules and conditions."
          }
        ],
        "quotationMatchPolicy": "unicode-typography-v1",
        "typographyNormalizedPassages": []
      },
      "5-source-4": {
        "type": "technical-doc",
        "title": "Virtual Private Networks Documentation",
        "publisher": "Netgate (pfSense)",
        "url": "https://docs.netgate.com/pfsense/en/latest/vpn/index.html",
        "language": "en",
        "jurisdiction": "Open-source project",
        "applicability": "pfSense firewall configuration for IPsec, OpenVPN, and WireGuard",
        "publicationDate": null,
        "effectiveDate": null,
        "redistribution": "metadata-and-short-passages",
        "id": "5-source-4",
        "byteDigest": "sha256:1000517d6560b099c10e1d02b60977f9ec72abb0542ceaabefc0d45cb8c1b01b",
        "textDigest": "sha256:857d2b9da9a8020205b0cefd474d82c07647627cd44956addf757b4d67f765f4",
        "finalUrl": "https://docs.netgate.com/pfsense/en/latest/vpn/index.html",
        "retrievedAt": "2026-10-15T21:24:44Z",
        "contentType": "text/html",
        "snapshotPath": "source-1000517d6560b099c10e1d02b60977f9ec72abb0542ceaabefc0d45cb8c1b01b.bin",
        "textPath": "source-857d2b9da9a8020205b0cefd474d82c07647627cd44956addf757b4d67f765f4.txt",
        "sourceStatus": "fetched-and-passage-checked",
        "passages": [
          {
            "id": "p1",
            "locator": "article/heading/page",
            "text": "VPNs provide a means of tunneling traffic through an encrypted connection, preventing it from being seen or modified in transit. pfSense® software offers several VPN options: IPsec, OpenVPN, WireGuard and L2TP. This section provides an overview of VPN usage, the pros and cons of each type of VPN, and how to decide which is the best fit for a particular environment."
          },
          {
            "id": "p2",
            "locator": "article/heading/page",
            "text": "PPTP relies upon MS-CHAPv2 which has been completely compromised. Intercepted traffic can be decrypted by a third party 100% of the time, so consider any traffic carried in PPTP unencrypted. Migrate to another VPN type as soon as possible."
          }
        ],
        "quotationMatchPolicy": "unicode-typography-v1",
        "typographyNormalizedPassages": []
      },
      "5-source-5": {
        "type": "technical-doc",
        "title": "Red Hat Enterprise Linux 9 Configuring firewalls and packet filters",
        "publisher": "Red Hat",
        "url": "https://docs.redhat.com/en/documentation/red_hat_enterprise_linux/9/pdf/configuring_firewalls_and_packet_filters/red_hat_enterprise_linux-9-configuring_firewalls_and_packet_filters-en-us.pdf",
